      "errorMessage": "<task id=\"ses_f0bee2cf1ffe9q9W3nw3p6rJ1R\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nResearch complete. Below is the full report. All paths are absolute; line numbers point at the key seams.\n\n---\n\n# 1. Object / record read-permission determination\n\n## Canonical hooks & utils\n\n| Artifact | Path | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `useObjectPermissions()` | `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/hooks/useObjectPermissions.ts` (L20) | Reads `currentUserWorkspaceState` → `currentUserWorkspace.objectsPermissions` (L21-22), builds `objectPermissionsByObjectMetadataId` map. Returns no boolean, only the map. |\n| `useObjectPermissionsForObject(objectMetadataId)` | `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/hooks/useObjectPermissionsForObject.ts` (L7) | Memoized wrapper over `getObjectPermissionsForObject`. |\n| `getObjectPermissionsForObject(map, id)` | `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-metadata/utils/getObjectPermissionsForObject.ts` (L5) | Pure. **Security caveat:** if no entry exists it returns all `can*ObjectRecords: true` (L17-28). A missing permission row means \"allowed\", so a stub must not treat \"unknown object id\" as the denial signal. |\n| `getObjectPermissionsFromMapByObjectMetadataId` | `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/settings/roles/role-permissions/objects-permissions/utils/getObjectPermissionsFromMapByObjectMetadataId.ts` (L11) | Same default-to-`true` behavior (L16-25). |\n| `ObjectPermissions` type | `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-shared/src/types/ObjectPermissions.ts` (L5) | Fields: `canReadObjectRecords`, `canUpdateObjectRecords`, `canSoftDeleteObjectRecords`, `canDestroyObjectRecords`, `restrictedFields`, `rowLevelPermissionPredicates`, `rowLevelPermissionPredicateGroups`. |\n| `useReadableObjectMetadataItems()` | `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-metadata/hooks/useReadableObjectMetadataItems.ts` (L7) | Filters active objects by `canReadObjectRecords`. |\n| `filterReadableActiveObjectMetadataItems` | `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-metadata/utils/filterReadableActiveObjectMetadataItems.ts` (L5, default-allow L20-22) | |\n| `objectMetadataItem.readableFields` / `updatableFields` | `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-metadata/utils/enrichObjectMetadataItemsWithPermissions.ts` (L47-52); selector `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-metadata/states/objectMetadataItemsWithFieldsSelector.ts` (L87) | Field-level read derived from `restrictedFields` → `getNonReadableFieldMetadataIdsFromObjectPermissions`. |\n\n**There is no hook named** `useHasObjectReadPermission`, `ObjectPermissionContext`, `isReadableObject`, or a `canReadObjectRecords()` function. The only idiom is reading `.canReadObjectRecords` off the permissions object (grep over `modules/object-record/hooks` confirms). `objectMetadataItem.isReadable` does not exist; only `readableFields`.\n\n## Consumption patterns in components\n\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/record-index/components/RecordIndexContainerGater.tsx` L51-57: `useObjectPermissions()` → `getObjectPermissionsForObject(...)` → `hasObjectReadPermissions`; L71-78 renders `RecordIndexEmptyStateNotShared` when false. Also hides the ViewBar (L113).\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/record-table/components/RecordTable.tsx` L30, L80: `objectPermissions.canReadObjectRecords &&` gates the table.\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/hooks/useFindOneRecord.ts` L48-61: `hasReadPermission` is passed to Apollo `skip`.\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/hooks/useFindManyRecords.ts` L87-95: same `skip` guard.\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/record-table-widget/components/RecordTableWidgetProvider.tsx` L134-136: returns `null` when `!canReadObjectRecords` (another safe-stub precedent).\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-metadata/utils/mapFieldMetadataToGraphQLQuery.ts` L86, L165, L217 and `mapObjectMetadataToGraphQLQuery.ts` L46: permission-aware query generation.\n\n---\n\n# 2. View access determination\n\n**There is no `canAccessView` / `useCanAccessView` / `viewPermissions` in the frontend** (repo-wide grep found zero). View access is a composite of three things:\n\n### a) Does the view exist for the current user? (state, not a network hook)\n- `useViewById(viewId)` — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/views/hooks/useViewById.ts` (L4): reads the metadata-store selector and returns `{ view: viewId ? view : undefined }`. `undefined` is the safe denial/not-found signal.\n- Selector: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/views/states/selectors/viewFromViewIdFamilySelector.ts` (L5).\n- `useGetCurrentViewOnly()` — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/views/hooks/useGetCurrentViewOnly.ts` (L6), reads `contextStoreCurrentViewIdComponentState`.\n- `useGetViewFromState()` — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/views/hooks/useGetViewFromState.ts` (L5), imperative store read.\n- Views list per object: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/views/states/selectors/viewsFromObjectMetadataItemFamilySelector.ts` (L7).\n- Aggregation from metadata store: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/views/states/selectors/viewsSelector.ts` (L14-115), joining `metadataStoreState` keys `views`, `viewFields`, `viewFilters`, `viewSorts`, `viewGroups`, `viewFilterGroups`, `viewFieldGroups`.\n\n### b) Can the user read the object the view is scoped to?\nUse `getObjectPermissionsForObject(map, view.objectMetadataId).canReadObjectRecords`. This is the actual read gate used by `RecordIndexContainerGater.tsx` (L52-57) and `getNonReadableInfoForViewField.ts` (L54-63). There is no view-specific object permission; the `view` data is metadata, not an object-record subject to `canReadObjectRecords`.\n\n### c) Does the view use fields/sorts/filters the user cannot read?\n- `useHasCurrentViewNonReadableFields(objectMetadataItem)` — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/record-index/hooks/useHasCurrentViewNonReadableFields.ts` (L20). Reads current view from state, compares `view.viewSorts` (L52) and `view.viewFilters` (L63) against `objectMetadataItem.readableFields` + `objectPermissionsByObjectMetadataId`.\n- Helper: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/record-index/utils/getNonReadableInfoForViewField.ts` (L8).\n- Subtitle copy: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/record-index/utils/getNonReadableViewFieldSubTitle.ts` (L5).\n- Consumed in `RecordIndexContainer.tsx` L41-49 and `RecordIndexViewBar.tsx` L20.\n\n### d) `PermissionFlagType.VIEWS` (create/modify, not read)\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/settings/roles/hooks/useHasPermissionFlag.ts` (L9).\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/views/hooks/useCanPersistViewChanges.ts` (L8-26): users without `VIEWS` may only persist `UNLISTED` (their own).\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/views/view-picker/components/ViewPickerContentEffect.tsx` (L79, L94-96) and `ViewPickerOptionDropdown.tsx` (L60).\n- Enum: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-shared/src/constants/PermissionFlagType.ts` (L18).\n\n### Server-side (why unauthorized views never reach the client)\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/view/services/view.service.ts` L378-394 `isViewVisibleToUser` (WORKSPACE visible to all; UNLISTED only creator), applied in `getFilteredFlatViews` L396-429.\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/view-permissions/services/view-access.service.ts` (L25, L50, L76, L104-156) — guards create/modify/child-entity access via `PermissionFlagType.VIEWS`.\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/view/exceptions/view.exception.ts` — `VIEW_CREATE_PERMISSION_DENIED` / `VIEW_MODIFY_PERMISSION_DENIED`.\n\n**Recommended denial predicate for an embedded-view block:** `view === undefined` OR `!getObjectPermissionsForObject(map, view.objectMetadataId).canReadObjectRecords` OR `useHasCurrentViewNonReadableFields(...).hasCurrentViewNonReadableFields`. Render a stub component in any of these cases.\n\n---\n\n# 3. Existing fallback / \"no access\" components\n\nBest direct precedents:\n\n- **`RecordIndexEmptyStateNotShared`** — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/record-index/components/RecordIndexEmptyStateNotShared.tsx` (L23-44). Renders `AnimatedPlaceholder type=\"notShared\"`, title `View not shared` / `Object not shared` (L32-40). Props: `nonReadableViewFieldInfo`. This is the closest match to \"safe stub for a view\".\n- **`ForbiddenFieldDisplay`** — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/record-field/ui/meta-types/display/components/ForbiddenFieldDisplay.tsx` (L25-33): lock icon + `<Trans>Not shared</Trans>`.\n- **`PageLayoutWidgetForbiddenDisplay`** — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/page-layout/widgets/components/PageLayoutWidgetForbiddenDisplay.tsx` (L12-50): `ForbiddenFieldDisplay` + tooltip; messages \"You do not have permission to access the ${objectName} object\" (L21) / field (L31-32) / widget (L36).\n- **`WidgetCardShell`** — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/page-layout/widgets/components/WidgetCardShell.tsx` (L130-148): `hasAccess ? <ErrorBoundary FallbackComponent={PageLayoutWidgetInvalidConfigDisplay}><WidgetContentRenderer/></ErrorBoundary> : <IconLock/>`. This is the cleanest \"render content or safe lock stub\" pattern; note it wraps content in `ErrorBoundary` too (L131-140).\n- **`useWidgetPermissions`** — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/page-layout/widgets/hooks/useWidgetPermissions.ts` (L15-84): returns `{ hasAccess, restriction }` from object read + `checkFieldPermissions`; `WidgetAccessDenialInfo` shape at `.../widgets/types/WidgetAccessDenialInfo`.\n- **`RecordIndexContainerGater`** — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/record-index/components/RecordIndexContainerGater.tsx` L71-78 (object-read denial → `RecordIndexEmptyStateNotShared`).\n- **`RecordIndexEmptyState`** — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/record-index/components/RecordIndexEmptyState.tsx` L69-78: \"You are not allowed to create records for this object\".\n- **`RecordTableWidgetProvider`** — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/record-table-widget/components/RecordTableWidgetProvider.tsx` L134-136: returns `null` on no read.\n- **`WorkspaceRouteUnavailable`** — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/app/routing/components/WorkspaceRouteUnavailable.tsx` (L16-28): \"This page isn't available.\" Used by pages as a safe route fallback: `RecordShowPage.tsx` L66-73, L146-157; `RecordIndexPage.tsx` L54-60.\n- **`NotFound` page** — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/pages/not-found/NotFound.tsx` (L44-76).\n- **A2E concrete precedent (PERMISSION_DENIED with preserved state)** — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/a2e-workspace/components/A2eWorkspaceTemplatePreview.tsx` L217-256 and L495-496; `isPermissionDenied = errorCode === 'PERMISSION_DENIED'` (L231), disables apply but keeps the choice (L250-256).\n- **Error boundaries** — `AppErrorBoundary` (L50-130), `AppRootErrorFallback`, `AppFullScreenErrorFallback`, `AppPageErrorFallback` under `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/error-handler/components/`.\n\nNote: there is no component literally named `RecordTableNoRecordGroupEmptyState` or `PermissionDenied` in this fork; the table empty state is `RecordTableEmptyState` → `RecordIndexEmptyState` (`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/record-table/empty-state/components/RecordTableEmptyState.tsx` L7).\n\n---\n\n# 4. BlockNote module structure & registration seams\n\nDirectory: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/blocknote-editor/`\n\n```\nblocks/            BookmarkBlock.tsx, CalloutBlock.tsx, FileBlock.tsx,\n                   MentionInlineContent.tsx, PageLinkBlock.tsx,\n                   TableOfContentsBlock.tsx, TodoTaskBlock.tsx, Schema.ts\ncomponents/        BlockEditor.tsx, CustomSlashMenu*.tsx, CustomSideMenu*.tsx,\n                   CustomMentionMenu.tsx, CustomAddBlockItem.tsx,\n                   LinkToRecordPicker.tsx, LinkToRecordSlashMenuItem.tsx\ncontexts/          BlockEditorDocumentContext.ts,\n                   BlockEditorCompoponeInstanceContext.ts   (sic: typo in filename)\nhooks/             useAttachmentSync.ts, useReplaceBlockEditorContent.ts\nstates/            isSlashMenuOpenComponentState.ts\ntypes/             types.ts\nutils/             getSlashMenu.ts, slashMenuItemDefinitions.ts,\n                   slashMenuGroups.ts, getColumnListBlock.ts,\n                   buildBookmarkCardFromUrl.ts, buildChildDocumentInput.ts,\n                   buildTaskFromTodoBlockInput.ts, getFileEmbedKind.ts,\n                   parseInitialBlocknote.ts, prepareBodyWithSignedUrls.ts, ...\nimport/            adapters/parseHtmlWithBlockNote.ts + utils/ + __tests__/\nexport/            components/BlockEditorExportMenu.tsx + utils/\neditor-status/     components/BlockEditorStatusBar.tsx, hooks/, states/, utils/\nco-editing/        components/, hooks/useDocumentCursors.ts, utils/\ncomments/          EditorCommentsThreadStore.ts, hooks/, utils/\nversion-history/   EditorVersionHistoryStore.ts, components/, hooks/, states/, utils/\nconstants/         BlockEditorGlobalHotkeysConfig.ts\n```\n\n## Where a new custom block registers\n\n1. **Block spec** — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/blocknote-editor/blocks/Schema.ts` L18-33: add entry to `blockSpecs` (L20-28). Pattern to follow: `createReactBlockSpec({ type, propSchema, content }, { render, toExternalHTML })` as in `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/blocknote-editor/blocks/PageLinkBlock.tsx` L114-139.\n2. **Slash-menu item** — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/blocknote-editor/utils/getSlashMenu.ts` L110-159 (`customItems`, each with `onItemClick: insertOrUpdateBlockForSlashMenu(editor, { type, props })`, e.g. L131-138) and the definition key in `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/blocknote-editor/utils/slashMenuItemDefinitions.ts` L193-275 (`SLASH_MENU_CUSTOM_ITEM_DEFINITIONS`).\n3. **Menu group** — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/blocknote-editor/utils/slashMenuGroups.ts` (`SLASH_MENU_GROUP_LABELS`, `SLASH_MENU_GROUP_ORDER`).\n4. **Schema wiring at editor creation** — `BLOCK_SCHEMA` is passed to `useCreateBlockNote` in the A2E document/note rich-text editor: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/record-field/ui/meta-types/input/components/RichTextFieldEditor.tsx` L198-210 (`schema: BLOCK_SCHEMA`). Headless import parser: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/blocknote-editor/import/adapters/parseHtmlWithBlockNote.ts` L9. Note the standalone dashboard editor uses a **separate** schema `DASHBOARD_BLOCK_SCHEMA` (`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/page-layout/widgets/standalone-rich-text/constants/DashboardBlockSchema.ts`, used at `StandaloneRichTextEditorContent.tsx` L64) — a new block added only to `Schema.ts` will not appear there.\n\n## Context\n\n- `BlockEditorDocumentContext` defined at `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/blocknote-editor/contexts/BlockEditorDocumentContext.ts` L7 — `createContext<string | null>(null)`, holds the `document` record id.\n- Provided in `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/blocknote-editor/components/BlockEditor.tsx` L305 (`value={documentRecordId ?? null}`, prop declared L42), closed L358.\n- Consumed via `useContext(BlockEditorDocumentContext)` in `PageLinkBlock.tsx` L49.\n- Second context: `BlockEditorComponentInstanceContext` (`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/blocknote-editor/contexts/BlockEditorCompoponeInstanceContext.ts` L3) for component-instance state scoping.\n\nA new block's `render`/`render` inner component is a normal React component, so it can call `useObjectPermissionsForObject`, `useViewById`, `useObjectMetadataItems`, etc. directly.\n\n---\n\n# 5. GraphQL hooks for object metadata and views\n\n## Object metadata\n- `useObjectMetadataItem({ objectNameSingular })` — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-metadata/hooks/useObjectMetadataItem.ts` L10. **Throws `ObjectMetadataItemNotFoundError` when absent** (L26-31) — do not call it unguarded inside a block unless wrapped in an error boundary.\n- `useObjectMetadataItemById({ objectId })` — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-metadata/hooks/useObjectMetadataItemById.ts` L5. **Also throws** (L16-21).\n- Non-throwing alternatives: `useObjectMetadataItems()` — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-metadata/hooks/useObjectMetadataItems.ts` L4; `useFilteredObjectMetadataItems()` — `.../hooks/useFilteredObjectMetadataItems.ts` L5 (has `findObjectMetadataItemById`, L49-52); `useReadableObjectMetadataItems()` (above). Use these for a safe stub.\n- Network source: `FIND_MANY_OBJECT_METADATA_ITEMS` loaded in `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/metadata-store/hooks/useLoadStaleMetadataEntities.ts` L77-93.\n\n## Record\n- `useFindOneRecord` — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/hooks/useFindOneRecord.ts` L16. Skips the query when the object is unreadable (L52-61); returns `{ record, loading, error, refetch }`.\n- `useFindManyRecords` — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/hooks/useFindManyRecords.ts` L36. Same `bound` skip (L91-95).\n- Show-page wrapper: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/record-show/hooks/useRecordShowPageResource.ts` L7-33.\n\n## Views (important: no per-id record hook)\nViews are **metadata**, loaded into `metadataStoreState`, not fetched with `useFindOneRecord`. There is no single-view GraphQL query (`GetViewDocument`/`view(id)` does not exist in `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/generated-metadata/graphql.ts`; only `getViews`/`FindManyViews`).\n- Read a view by id from state: `useViewById(viewId)` (above) / `useGetViewFromState()`.\n- Queries:\n  - `FIND_ALL_VIEWS` — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/views/graphql/queries/findAllViews.ts` L4.\n  - `FIND_MANY_VIEWS` — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/views/graphql/queries/findManyViews.ts` L4.\n  - `FIND_TABLE_WIDGET_VIEWS` — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/views/graphql/queries/findTableWidgetViews.ts` L6.\n  - `FIND_FIELDS_WIDGET_VIEWS` — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/views/graphql/queries/findFieldsWidgetViews.ts` L6.\n  - Fragment with `viewFields/viewSorts/viewFilters/viewGroups/...`: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/views/graphql/fragments/viewFragment`.\n- Loader that fetches all four and splits relations into store keys: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/metadata-store/hooks/useLoadStaleMetadataEntities.ts` L95-145 (uses generated `FindAllViewsDocument`, `FindFieldsWidgetViewsDocument`, `FindTableWidgetViewsDocument`).\n- Minimal bootstrap query returning `views { id type key objectMetadataId }`: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/metadata-store/graphql/queries/findMinimalMetadata.ts` L17-22, executed by `useLoadMinimalMetadata` L16-101.\n\n---\n\n## Key takeaways for the embedded-view block\n\n1. Resolve the view with `useViewById(viewId)` (state); `undefined` covers \"not found\" and \"filtered out by permission\". Prefer non-throwing `useFilteredObjectMetadataItems().findObjectMetadataItemById(...)` over `useObjectMetadataItem`/`...ById` to avoid raw errors.\n2. Deny if `view` is undefined, if `getObjectPermissionsForObject(map, view.objectMetadataId).canReadObjectRecords` is false (via `useObjectPermissions`/`useObjectPermissionsForObject`), or if `useHasCurrentViewNonReadableFields(...).hasCurrentViewNonReadableFields` is true.\n3. Render a stub using the existing safe patterns: `RecordIndexEmptyStateNotShared` (view/object not shared), `WorkspaceRouteUnavailable` (route unavailable), or `ForbiddenFieldDisplay`/`PageLayoutWidgetForbiddenDisplay` + `IconLock` as in `WidgetCardShell` L130-148. Wrap any content that can throw (metadata lookups, GraphQL errors) in an `ErrorBoundary` as `WidgetCardShell` does.\n4. Beware `getObjectPermissionsForObject` defaulting to `true` for unknown metadata ids — always combine with an explicit \"view/object exists\" check.\n5. To add the block: register the spec in `blocks/Schema.ts` L20-28, add the slash item in `utils/getSlashMenu.ts` L110-159 plus `utils/slashMenuItemDefinitions.ts` L193, and remember the dashboard editor uses `DASHBOARD_BLOCK_SCHEMA` separately.\n</task_result>\n</task>",
