onentInstanceContext`: `.../record-table/components/RecordTableComponentInstance.tsx:15`; context file `.../record-table/states/context/RecordTableComponentInstanceContext.ts:3`.\n- `RecordTableContextProvider` (React context, per-table config incl. `onRecordIdentifierClick`): `.../record-table/components/RecordTableContextProvider.tsx:28`, context type `.../record-table/contexts/RecordTableContext.ts:18`.\n- `RecordBoardContext` + `RecordBoardComponentInstanceContext`: provided in `RecordBoardContainer.tsx:68,79`.\n- `RecordCalendarContextProvider`: `RecordCalendarContainer.tsx:27`.\n\n### Minimal provider tree a host needs (derived from `RecordTableWidgetProvider.tsx:138-184`)\n1. `RecordTableWidgetContext.Provider` (only if persisting draft/edits; can be skipped read-only)\n2. `ContextStoreComponentInstanceContext.Provider` (`:140`) — required for `contextStoreCurrentViewId` and by `useOpenRecordFromIndexView`\n3. Context-store init effect (`RecordTableWidgetContextStoreInitEffect`, `:147`)\n4. `RecordIndexContextProvider` (`:152`) — with `recordIndexId`, `viewBarInstanceId`, object metadata, `recordFieldByFieldMetadataItemId`, `labelIdentifierFieldMetadataItem`, field maps\n5. `ViewComponentInstanceContext.Provider instanceId={recordIndexId}` (`:169`)\n6. `RecordComponentInstanceContextsWrapper componentInstanceId={recordIndexId}` (`:172`)\n7. View-load effect (`RecordTableWidgetViewLoadEffect`, `:175`) → calls `loadRecordIndexStates`\n8. The view component (`RecordTableWidget` / `RecordBoardWidget` / `RecordCalendarWidget`)\n\n`recordIndexId` is just `` `${objectNamePlural}-${viewId}` ``: `.../object-record/utils/getRecordIndexIdFromObjectNamePluralAndViewId.ts:1`. `RecordTableWidgetProvider` computes it at `:55-63` (optional `instanceIdSuffix` to disambiguate multiple embeds of the same view).\n\n---\n\n## 3. How a specific view is identified/selected\n\nThere is **no `currentViewIdComponentState`**; the canonical atom is:\n- `contextStoreCurrentViewIdComponentState`: `.../context-store/states/contextStoreCurrentViewIdComponentState.ts:4` (component-scoped to `ContextStoreComponentInstanceContext`).\n\nReading/deriving:\n- `viewFromViewIdFamilySelector` `{ viewId }` → `.../views/states/selectors/viewFromViewIdFamilySelector.ts:5`, backed by `viewsByIdMapSelector.ts:5` and `viewsSelector.ts:14` (reads `metadataStoreState` `'views'`).\n- `indexViewIdFromObjectMetadataItemFamilySelector` `{ objectMetadataItemId }` — the `ViewKey.INDEX` view: `.../views/states/selectors/indexViewIdFromObjectMetadataItemFamilySelector.ts:5`.\n- `viewsFromObjectMetadataItemFamilySelector` `{ objectMetadataItemId }` — all non-widget views of an object, sorted: `.../views/states/selectors/viewsFromObjectMetadataItemFamilySelector.ts:7`.\n- Hooks: `useViewById(viewId)` `.../views/hooks/useViewById.ts:4`; `useGetCurrentViewOnly()` `.../views/hooks/useGetCurrentViewOnly.ts:6` (reads the context-store view id).\n\nURL / user selection:\n- `RouteContextStoreProvider.tsx:15-38` resolves a view id in priority: `?viewId` query param → last visited → index view → first available (`:107-112`).\n- `useSetViewInUrl` / `setViewInUrl` writes `?viewId=`: `.../views/hooks/useSetViewInUrl.ts:6`; `useChangeView` calls it: `.../views/hooks/useChangeView.ts:6`.\n\nProgrammatic selection (the embed path):\n- Set `contextStoreCurrentViewId` via `RecordTableWidgetContextStoreInitEffect`: `.../record-table-widget/components/RecordTableWidgetContextStoreInitEffect.tsx:31-34`.\n- Then hydrate scoped states with `useLoadRecordIndexStates().loadRecordIndexStates(view, objectMetadataItem, { recordIndexId })`: `.../record-index/hooks/useLoadRecordIndexStates.ts:225-391`; called from `RecordTableWidgetViewLoadEffect.tsx:81`.\n- `loadRecordIndexStates` sets `recordIndexViewTypeState`, filters/sorts/fields, group-by field, calendar field, kanban width, etc. (`:314-390`). It resolves `recordIndexId` from `options.recordIndexId ?? ambientViewInstanceId ?? namePlural-viewId` (`:150-156`, `:270-276`).\n- Types: `ViewType` enum `packages/twenty-shared/src/types/ViewType.ts:1`; `ViewKey`/`ViewKey.INDEX` used above; `ViewTypeDefaultIcons.ts:11`; widget layouts `.../page-layout/widgets/record-table/types/RecordTableWidgetLayoutViewType.ts:14-87`.\n\nMetadata must be loaded before any of this: `viewsSelector.ts:17` reads `metadataStoreState` `'views'`, and `RouteContextStoreProvider.tsx:114-124` bails until `metadataStore.status === 'up-to-date'`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Existing read-only modes\n\nRead-only is **Jotai component-state driven, not a prop** on the containers. No `readOnly` prop exists on `RecordTableWithWrappers`, `RecordBoardContainer`, `RecordCalendarContainer`, or `RecordIndexTableContainer`.\n\n### Table states (all `.../record-table/states/`)\n- `isRecordTableCellsNonEditableComponentState.ts:4` (default `false`)\n- `isRecordTableColumnHeadersReadOnlyComponentState.ts:4`\n- `isRecordTableCheckboxColumnHiddenComponentState.ts:4`\n- `isRecordTableDragColumnHiddenComponentState.ts:4`\n- `isRecordTableColumnResizableComponentState.ts:4` (default `true`)\n- `isRecordTableEmptyStateHiddenComponentState.ts:4`\n\nSet together (synchronously, pre-paint) by `RecordTableWidgetStatesEffect.tsx:25-66`, with unmount reset (`:68-105`). Props surface: `RecordTableWidget` `isUIEditable=false`, `isEmptyStateHidden=false` (`RecordTableWidget.tsx:14-22`).\n\nConsumers: `RecordTableHeaderCell.tsx:42-43`, `RecordTableHeaderFirstCell.tsx:40-41`, `RecordTableHeaderDnd.tsx:22-42`, `RecordTableCellBaseContainer.tsx:18-83` (`isReadOnly` prop), etc.\n\nRow/field-level permission read-only (separate mechanism):\n- `useIsRecordReadOnly({ recordId, objectMetadataId })`: `.../read-only/hooks/useIsRecordReadOnly.ts:14`.\n- `useIsRecordFieldReadOnly(...)`: `.../read-only/hooks/useIsRecordFieldReadOnly.ts:14`.\n- Util `isRecordFieldReadOnly`: `.../read-only/utils/isRecordFieldReadOnly.ts`; `isRecordReadOnly`: `.../read-only/utils/isRecordReadOnly.ts`.\n- Applied in `RecordTableTr.tsx:48`, `RecordTableCellFieldContextGeneric.tsx:121-125`, `RecordBoardCardContextProvider.tsx:42-68`, `RecordBoardCardBody.tsx:89`, calendar cards.\n\n### Board\n- `isRecordBoardViewSettingsReadOnlyComponentState.ts:6` (hides view-settings/drag-select, keeps data editable)\n- `isRecordBoardCellsNonEditableComponentState.ts:4` (disables cell editing)\n- Set by `RecordBoardWidgetStatesEffect.tsx:27-36`, prop `RecordBoardWidget isUIEditable=false` (`RecordBoardWidget.tsx:14-20`).\n- Consumers: `RecordBoard.tsx:45-64`, `RecordBoardColumnHeader.tsx:143-268`, `RecordBoardColumnDndKitProvider.tsx:23-31`.\n\n### Calendar\n- `isRecordCalendarReadOnlyComponentState.ts:7` (no drag, no create, no layout switch)\n- Set by `RecordCalendarWidgetReadOnlyEffect.tsx:21-28`, prop `RecordCalendarWidget isReadOnly=true` (`RecordCalendarWidget.tsx:17-23`).\n\nNote: `RecordCalendarWidgetReadOnlyEffect` + `RecordTableWidgetStatesEffect` reset their flag on unmount specifically so it \"cannot leak into a later [table/calendar] mounted on the same instance id\" (`RecordTableWidgetStatesEffect.tsx:68-105`, `RecordCalendarWidgetReadOnlyEffect.tsx:24-28`). A BlockNote embed must do the same or use unique instance ids per embed.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Tests showing the minimal provider tree\n\n- `.../record-index/hooks/__tests__/useLoadRecordIndexStates.test.tsx:34-40` — wraps only `getJestMetadataAndApolloMocksWrapper(...)` then calls `loadRecordIndexStates(view, objectMetadataItem, { skipGlobalIndexStates: true, recordIndexId })`. This is the smallest known wrapper for driving view hydration.\n- `packages/twenty-front/src/testing/jest/getJestMetadataAndApolloMocksWrapper.tsx:44-67` — provider order: `JotaiProvider` → `SnackBarComponentInstanceContext` → `MockedProvider` → `RecordComponentInstanceContextsWrapper` → `ViewComponentInstanceContext` → `JestObjectMetadataItemSetter` → `ContextStoreComponentInstanceContext` → `JestContextStoreSetter`.\n- `.../testing/jest/getJestMetadataAndApolloMocksAndCommandMenuWrapper.tsx:50-82` — adds `ContextStoreComponentInstanceContext`, `CommandMenuComponentInstanceContext`, and `JestRecordIndexContextProviderWrapper`.\n- `.../testing/jest/JestRecordIndexContextProviderWrapper.tsx:26-57` — minimal `RecordIndexContext` tree: RecordFilterGroups + RecordFilters + RecordSorts instance contexts + `RecordIndexContextProvider` with derived field maps.\n- `.../testing/jest/JestContextStoreSetter.tsx:36-133` — seeds `contextStoreCurrentViewId`, object metadata id, view type, targeted-records rule, filters.\n- `.../record-index/hooks/__tests__/useRecordIndexIdFromCurrentContextStore.test.tsx:12-18` — same wrapper, asserts `recordIndexId = namePlural-viewId` and side-panel suffixing (`:45-47`, `:72-74`).\n- `.../page-layout/widgets/record-table/components/__tests__/RecordTableWidgetRendererContent.test.tsx:9-55` — mocks the provider/widgets to test only layout dispatch (shows the widget API contract).\n- `.../record-calendar/components/__tests__/RecordCalendar.test.tsx` — heavy `jest.mock` of dependencies; does not exercise the provider tree.\n- `.../pages/object-record/__tests__/RecordIndexPage.surface.test.tsx:45-47` — mocks `RecordIndexContainerGater` itself (surface routing only).\n\nGeneric test decorator (stories/e2e): `.../testing/decorators/PageDecorator.tsx:102` provides `ContextStoreComponentInstanceContext`; `ContextStoreDecorator.tsx:35`.\n\n---\n\n## Synthesis / seams for the BlockNote view-embed block\n\nThe closest existing template is the dashboard/widget stack:\n- Dispatcher: `.../page-layout/widgets/record-table/components/RecordTableWidgetRendererContent.tsx:37-111` (takes `objectMetadataId`, `viewId`, `widgetId`, `recordLimit`, `instanceIdSuffix`; maps layout → widget; passes `contextStoreViewType`).\n- Provider: `.../object-record/record-table-widget/components/RecordTableWidgetProvider.tsx:40-186`.\n- Read-only effects: `RecordTableWidgetStatesEffect.tsx`, `RecordBoardWidgetStatesEffect.tsx`, `RecordCalendarWidgetReadOnlyEffect.tsx`.\n\nBlockNote integration points in this repo:\n- Schema registration: `.../blocknote-editor/blocks/Schema.ts:18-33` (`BLOCK_SCHEMA`, used by `BlockEditor`) and `.../page-layout/widgets/standalone-rich-text/constants/DashboardBlockSchema.ts:3-14` (`DASHBOARD_BLOCK_SCHEMA`). A new block spec must be added to whichever schema(s) should expose it.\n- Custom block example (atom block with props): `.../blocknote-editor/blocks/TodoTaskBlock.tsx:59`.\n- Slash menu item: `.../blocknote-editor/utils/getSlashMenu.ts:93-161` + definitions `.../blocknote-editor/utils/slashMenuItemDefinitions.ts:193` + group list `.../blocknote-editor/utils/slashMenuGroups.ts:7` (`'bureau'`/`'syna'` groups available).\n- Editor host context: `.../page-layout/widgets/standalone-rich-text/components/StandaloneRichTextEditorContent.tsx:34` is the same shape as `BlockEditor.tsx:183`.\n\nGotchas to plan around:\n- `RecordTableWidgetProvider.tsx:97` calls `useIsPageLayoutInEditMode()` which uses `createRequiredContext` (`.../page-layout/contexts/PageLayoutEditModeContext.ts:7`, throwing behavior `.../utils/createRequiredContext.ts:7-17`). So reusing `RecordTableWidgetProvider` outside a page layout requires wrapping with `PageLayoutEditModeProviderContext` (`{ isInEditMode: false }`) or writing an equivalent embed provider. `PageLayoutComponentInstanceContext` is optional (`useComponentInstanceStateContext`, `RecordTableWidgetProvider.tsx:93`, falls back to `MISSING_RECORD_TABLE_WIDGET_PAGE_LAYOUT_ID`).\n- `RecordTableWithWrappers.tsx:61,66` hardcodes `useOpenRecordFromIndexView()` and `useSelectAllRows`. For a read-only embed, prefer `RecordTableContextProvider` directly (`RecordTableContextProvider.tsx:20-98`) with a custom/no-op `onRecordIdentifierClick`, or accept that record clicks navigate.\n- `RecordBoardContainer.tsx:63-65` and `RecordIndexCalendarContainer.tsx:12-17` return `null` until the view's group/calendar field is hydrated by `loadRecordIndexStates`.\n- View metadata must be loaded (`viewsSelector.ts:14-17`); `RouteContextStoreProvider.tsx:114-124` gates on `metadataStore.status === 'up-to-date'`.\n- No `GALLERY` view type exists in this fork (`packages/twenty-shared/src/types/ViewType.ts:1-11`); the equivalent is `LIST` (`RecordListWidget`, intrinsically read-only, `RecordTableWidgetLayoutViewType.ts:84-86`).\n</task_result>\n</task>"
